Your study suggests that investment in education, career services, and training programs will have a substantial impact on improving the economic status of individuals and communities. Please elaborate on your recommendations for improving community literacy and lifelong learning.

The study recommends that significant funding be appropriated to prepare a qualified and skilled workforce and develop a ‘lifelong learning community’ through:

- The Mississippi Community and Adult Education Program through community and adult literacy programs;
- The Education for Employment Enhancement Program;
- Career and Technical Education Programs;
- Additional funded investments in K-12 education and postsecondary education, including the incentive to promote completion of postsecondary education through continuous support programs; and
- The university system to enhance their workforce development programs.

The goal is to have a trained, prepared, and ready-to-earn workforce that can fill any open positions that future development and job opportunities may require.  Creating a skilled workforce also ensures that residents can take advantage of opportunities with our universities, industrial, and corporate partners.  These investment strategies will develop programs to:

- Assess the current workforce education levels, preparation, and skills levels;
